Players now get a limited stock of each block type. The server side is done: BlockPlacement.server.luau gives everyone 20 of each and fires the StockChanged remote (in ReplicatedStorage) with (blockTypeName, count) whenever one of the player's counts changes, including once per block type when they join. Nothing on the client uses it yet.

On the client, keep the stock in Charm, like the selected block type in BlockPlacer already is. Then:
- show each block type's count on its hotbar tile, and gray out a tile when its count is 0;
- show "<n> left" for the selected block type just above the hotbar;
- make BlockPlacer stop asking the server to place a block type the player has none of.

The client code is in src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts (BlockPlacer.luau, BlockPicker.luau, Main.client.luau). Add a module there for the stock if you need one.
